# Learning in Science: A Comparison of Deep and Surface Approaches.

**Authors:** Chin, Christine, Brown, David E.

## Abstract
Explores the differences between deep and surface approaches to learning science. Findings indicate that the deep-surface learning differences fall into five categories: (1) generative thinking; (2) nature of explanations; (3) asking questions; (4) metacognitive activity; and (5) approach to tasks. Suggests that teachers can encourage a deep learning approach by providing prompts and contextualized scaffolding. (Contains 89 references.) (Author/WRM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ602316

